  "id": "COMPOUND:16006 - PROTEIN:4991",
  "verbalization": "Spiroquinazoline is implicated in the interaction with P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Gentiakochianin-1-O-Glucoside and Nonan-2R-ol. These compounds, in turn, share a common target of HS27. The evidence suggests that Spiroquinazoline may act through a shared mechanism, targeting P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, which is a key mediator in various biological processes. The presence of multiple pathways leading to HS27 indicates that Spiroquinazoline may exert its effects through a common intermediate, P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, thereby establishing a potential link between Spiroquinazoline and HS27. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1 as a central node in the molecular network involving Spiroquinazoline and HS27.",
